---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { t } from '../../i18n';

const cvUrl = 'https://drive.google.com/uc?export=download&id=1WLq4NZn23nQbU_lBJup3fZNlmujHMa5X';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={t('about.title')}
  description="About Gianclaudio Moura Carella, a software engineer working on backend systems, cloud architecture, and AI."
>
  <section class="page-head section">
    <p class="eyebrow">{t('about.eyebrow')}</p>
    <h1>Gianclaudio Moura Carella</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Software engineer with 14+ years of experience in backend development and cloud-native
      solutions. I currently work as a senior software engineer at Sage and as founder and AI
      engineer at Allerac. I live in Barcelona.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section prose-grid">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Profile</p>
      <h2>Backend systems, cloud architecture, and applied AI.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-stack">
      <p>
        I have strong experience designing scalable, secure, and maintainable APIs and services,
        using cloud architecture. I care about clean code, SOLID design, TDD, and CI/CD pipelines,
        and I am interested in using technology to solve real-world problems — including AI
        technologies and chat capabilities.
      </p>
      <p>
        I distill technical complexity into clear solutions, help streamline team processes, and
        work across stakeholders. I adapt quickly, am comfortable wearing multiple hats, and I
        invest in work that matters.
      </p>
      <p>
        My career has spanned different stages of software development, from writing code by hand to
        building systems with AI. I believe the role of the software engineer is changing, but we
        are still turning ideas into systems — now also through natural language.
      </p>
      <p>I speak English, Spanish, and Portuguese.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-label={t('about.ledgerLabel')}>
    <div class="about-ledger">
      <article>
        <span>01</span>
        <h3>Sage — Data &amp; AI</h3>
        <p class="experience-role"><span class="experience-role-phrase">AI Engineer</span></p>
        <p>April 2026 – present · Barcelona, Spain</p>
        <h4>AI Infrastructure &amp; Governance (in development)</h4>
        <p>
          Contributing to AI infrastructure designed to support governance across Sage, with usage
          monitoring and centralized access to tools and Model Context Protocol (MCP) servers. The
          aim is company-wide support. The project is in development.
        </p>
        <h4>Content Hub</h4>
        <p>
          Contributing as a backend engineer, including AWS infrastructure support, to a shared
          content hub with semantic search over product-specific knowledge, so Sage products can
          retrieve validated content to ground AI responses and reduce the risk of hallucination.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>02</span>
        <h3>Sage — CloudOps</h3>
        <p class="experience-role">
          <span class="experience-role-phrase">Senior Software Engineer</span>
        </p>
        <p>December 2020 – March 2026 · Barcelona, Spain</p>
        <p>
          I led and contributed to global cloud migration initiatives, virtualizing 20+ on-premises
          products. I architected scalable backend APIs and microservices, automated infrastructure
          with Terraform and ARM templates, and applied TDD, SOLID, and clean-code practices with
          thorough code reviews. I collaborated with cross-functional international teams to refine
          requirements and improve processes.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>03</span>
        <h3>Allerac</h3>
        <p class="experience-role">
          Founder and <span class="experience-role-phrase">AI Engineer</span>
        </p>
        <p>June 2025 – present · Barcelona, Spain</p>
        <p>
          I am building a self-hosted AI agent platform, with isolated units and a chat that can run
          on a public website, using TypeScript and Next.js. The public repository is
          <a href="https://github.com/Allerac/allerac-one">Allerac/allerac-one</a>.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>04</span>
        <h3>Mercado Libre</h3>
        <p class="experience-role"><span class="experience-role-phrase">Software Engineer</span></p>
        <p>November 2019 – December 2020</p>
        <p>
          I developed backend services for marketing automation and experimentation platforms using
          .NET and containerized microservices. I contributed to container orchestration and
          deployment pipelines, improving scalability, reliability, and observability, and took part
          in architectural discussions, code reviews, and automated testing.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>05</span>
        <h3>Panamerican Quality Software</h3>
        <p class="experience-role">
          Tech Lead and <span class="experience-role-phrase">Senior Software Engineer</span>
        </p>
        <p>January 2016 – November 2019 · Buenos Aires, Argentina</p>
        <p>
          As a full-stack engineer I led the migration of legacy products from VBS to C# for banks,
          using .NET and Angular. I worked directly with clients on specifications, and after the
          migration I led the C# developers team with technical guidance and mentoring. I also
          contributed to architectural decisions that improved performance and maintainability.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>06</span>
        <h3>Avanade</h3>
        <p class="experience-role"><span class="experience-role-phrase">Software Engineer</span></p>
        <p>June 2012 – December 2016 · São Paulo, Brazil</p>
        <p>
          I began as an intern on the Transport Insurance team, working on the Mapfre Connect
          Calculator in .NET. I collaborated with client analysts on requirements and system
          improvements, and later managed and coordinated an offshore development team, addressing
          blockers and supporting knowledge transfer between onshore and offshore members.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section prose-grid">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Education</p>
      <h2>Studies.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-stack">
      <p>
        <strong>Postgraduate in Cloud Computing Architecture</strong> · 2026 – present · Universitat Politècnica
        de Catalunya (UPC), Barcelona. Advanced studies in cloud computing architecture, with a focus
        on designing and implementing scalable, secure, and cost-effective cloud solutions, including
        modern cloud platforms, infrastructure as code, microservices, and cloud-native application development.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Software Development &amp; Analysis (BFA)</strong> · 2010 – 2015 · FATEC Baixada Santista
        Rubens Lara, Santos, Brazil. Analysis, design, documentation, specification, testing, implementation,
        and maintenance of computer information systems, with attention to quality, usability, robustness,
        integrity, and security.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>International Relations</strong> · 2004 – 2007 · Centro Universitário Lusiadas. I studied
        for three years of a four-year programme and did not complete the degree.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section prose-grid">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Skills</p>
      <h2>Tools and methods.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-stack">
      <p>
        <strong>Backend &amp; architecture:</strong> .NET and C#, TypeScript, RESTful APIs, and distributed
        systems, including microservices, event-driven architectures, and modular monoliths, with SOLID
        principles, TDD, unit and integration testing, and SpecFlow. I also work with Angular and React.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Applied AI:</strong> Agents, retrieval-augmented generation (RAG), semantic search, evaluation
        and testing of agents, and AI governance.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Cloud &amp; operations:</strong> Microsoft Azure and AWS, infrastructure as code with
        Terraform, CI/CD, Docker, and Kubernetes, plus identity with Microsoft Entra ID (Azure AD) and
        OAuth/OpenID.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section prose-grid about-closing">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Contact</p>
      <h2>How to reach me.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-stack">
      <p>
        Email: <a href="mailto:gianclaudio.gc@gmail.com">gianclaudio.gc@gmail.com</a><br />
        Phone: <a href="tel:+34645863188">+34 645 863 188</a><br />
        Location: Barcelona
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="https://github.com/GianclaudioCarella">GitHub</a>
        ·
        <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/gianclaudiocarella/">LinkedIn</a>
        ·
        <a href={cvUrl}>Download CV</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
